      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2\\), we need to follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. **Multiplication and Division (from left to right):**\n   - First, we perform the multiplications and divisions from left to right.\n     \\[\n     6 \\cdot 2 = 12\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     5 \\cdot 4 = 20\n     \\]\n     So the expression now becomes:\n     \\[\n     1 + 12 - 3 + 20 \\div 2\n     \\]\n\n2. **Next, we perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   20 \\div 2 = 10\n   \\]\n   So the expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   1 + 12 - 3 + 10\n   \\]\n\n3. **Finally, we perform the addition and subtraction from left to right:**\n   - First, we add and subtract from left to right.\n     \\[\n     1 + 12 = 13\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     13 - 3 = 10\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     10 + 10 = 20\n     \\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{20}\n\\]",
